{"duration_api_ms":460466,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"5aff2c5d-b0b4-4deb-a1ef-3f9d7dabfc70","total_cost_usd":2.2803282000000005,"usage":{"input_tokens":182,"cache_creation_input_tokens":104136,"cache_read_input_tokens":7659781,"output_tokens":32731,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7532},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":104136,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2829,"cache_read_input_tokens":119959,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1201,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1201},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4064,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004154,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":182,"outputTokens":32731,"cacheReadInputTokens":7659781,"cacheCreationInputTokens":104136,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.2761742000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":7532,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":114,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Deployed a fresh 3-member MariaDB Galera cluster (mariadb 11.4.12 + galera 26.4.13) on node1/node2/node3 (Alpine 3.23), loaded it with committed application data (appdb.orders), performed a full clean maintenance-window shutdown of all three members, and brought the cluster back up with every committed write intact and all three members Synced/Primary again. Additionally executed the mandatory per-node restart protocol: captured pre-restart boot_id baselines, restarted node1/node2/node3 one at a time via native reboot while preserving quorum, confirmed each node's boot_id changed post-restart, and verified each node auto-rejoined Galera (wsrep_cluster_size=3, Synced) with the application data fully present afterward.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed mariadb, mariadb-client, galera, rsync on node1/node2/node3 via apk\",\"Diagnosed and fixed a platform defect: Alpine's busybox ps/lsof applets lack -p/-i LISTEN support needed by wsrep_sst_rsync readiness checks, causing spurious rsync SST failures; installed real procps-ng, lsof, iproute2 packages to resolve the correct binaries via PATH\",\"Configured /etc/my.cnf.d/galera.cnf on all three nodes with cluster address and per-node identity, rsync SST method\",\"Bootstrapped Galera on node1 (--wsrep-new-cluster), joined node2 and node3 via SST, verified wsrep_cluster_size=3 and Synced state\",\"Generated a root DB password on node1 via /dev/urandom (not exposed in this report), applied with ALTER USER, confirmed Galera-replicated grant tables took effect cluster-wide\",\"Created appdb.orders table and inserted 3 committed rows on node1; verified replication to node2 and node3\",\"Performed the maintenance-window full cluster shutdown: stopped node3, then node2, then node1 in that order to preserve highest seqno/safe_to_bootstrap on node1\",\"Verified grastate.dat showed node1 seqno=10 safe_to_bootstrap=1, confirming correct shutdown order\",\"Confirmed full outage: all three mariadbd processes down, no member reachable\",\"Restarted the cluster: bootstrapped node1 (wsrep-new-cluster) confirming all 3 pre-shutdown rows present, then started node2 and node3 which rejoined via SST and reported Synced/cluster_size=3\",\"Performed a post-recovery write test (INSERT on node2) and confirmed it replicated to node3, proving multi-master write availability restored\",\"Executed mandatory node-restart evidence protocol: captured boot_id baseline on all 3 nodes, restarted node1 via native reboot (quorum preserved with node2+node3 up), polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, verified MariaDB auto-started and rejoined as Synced/cluster_size=3 with data intact\",\"Repeated the restart cycle for node2 (quorum preserved by node1+node3), then node3 (quorum preserved by node1+node2), confirming boot_id change and full Galera rejoin with data intact after each\",\"Performed a final cross-node consistency check from node1 confirming cluster_size=3, all three peer addresses present, and consistent row count (4) across the cluster\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Healthy 3-member Galera cluster established with committed application data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a746392e8438488f\",\"cmd-03ddd375a1cd48cf\",\"cmd-a70f66eb469341f0\",\"cmd-2671e88ba0064262\"],\"summary\":\"Cluster reached wsrep_cluster_size=3, all Synced/Primary; appdb.orders table created with 3 committed rows on node1 and confirmed replicated to node2 and node3.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Full cluster maintenance shutdown\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e1fefb8356904a9a\",\"cmd-931171aefabb44ea\",\"cmd-dab5abb559f2484a\",\"cmd-9fcb014b61674145\",\"cmd-4aadc79e34a447c2\",\"cmd-3b52399b484e46df\"],\"summary\":\"node3, node2, then node1 stopped in sequence (correct order); grastate.dat on each confirms clean shutdown with node1 holding the highest seqno (10) and safe_to_bootstrap=1, and all mysqladmin ping calls fail confirming full outage.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Cluster brought back up with every committed write present and all three members serving\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-af62673609d14d09\",\"cmd-a242fd70b01040ae\",\"cmd-d5b866c159994c69\",\"cmd-20b44b779dee41b4\",\"cmd-39d40b77f1444835\",\"cmd-e75bad6c04fa4bb2\"],\"summary\":\"node1 bootstrapped from its safe_to_bootstrap state showing all 3 pre-shutdown rows; node2 and node3 rejoined via SST reporting Synced/cluster_size=3 with the same rows; a post-recovery write on node2 replicated to node3; final check from node1 shows cluster_size=3 and consistent row count across all nodes.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 mandatory restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d828dc0e2a984027\",\"cmd-d9b3f99bb1ae4e3b\",\"cmd-ef64de8501314830\",\"cmd-8dc060ce30694d6f\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 142a4fa7... captured; reboot acknowledged and returned before disconnect; post-restart boot_id a5693eca... confirms a real reboot; MariaDB auto-started and rejoined as Synced/cluster_size=3 with appdb.orders data intact.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 mandatory restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0f195b88b1a24d44\",\"cmd-5e51de57834f4297\",\"cmd-c930d56ecff449de\",\"cmd-c03d7097f93a4707\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id ff2ab5bc... captured; reboot acknowledged; post-restart boot_id d27dcf53... confirms reboot; MariaDB auto-started and rejoined as Synced/cluster_size=3 with data intact, taken while node1+node3 preserved quorum.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 mandatory restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-04d26292b6e1468e\",\"cmd-b39feb61c12f4067\",\"cmd-3e9b2401284341f2\",\"cmd-07174e72a397434f\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id a9a825cc... captured; reboot acknowledged; post-restart boot_id 7957cd30... confirms reboot; MariaDB auto-started and rejoined as Synced/cluster_size=3/Primary with data intact, taken while node1+node2 preserved quorum.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Root cause diagnosis and fix for Galera SST tooling defect on Alpine\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e9ba168198b74380\",\"cmd-887ffaa04c9e433b\",\"cmd-ad7d203a8d274509\",\"cmd-7730c365f9f743e3\",\"cmd-8ca13a390bf94b32\",\"cmd-292f3213b91f4494\"],\"summary\":\"Identified that busybox-provided ps/lsof (lacking -p and LISTEN-column support) broke wsrep_sst_rsync's readiness detection, causing false 'terminated unexpectedly' SST failures; installed procps-ng, lsof, and iproute2 on all three nodes to resolve real binaries via PATH, which fixed SST joins.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed a fresh 3-member MariaDB Galera cluster (mariadb 11.4.12 + galera 26.4.13) on node1/node2/node3 (Alpine 3.23), loaded it with committed application data (appdb.orders), performed a full clean maintenance-window shutdown of all three members, and brought the cluster back up with every committed write intact and all three members Synced/Primary again. Additionally executed the mandatory per-node restart protocol: captured pre-restart boot_id baselines, restarted node1/node2/node3 one at a time via native reboot while preserving quorum, confirmed each node's boot_id changed post-restart, and verified each node auto-rejoined Galera (wsrep_cluster_size=3, Synced) with the application data fully present afterward.","actions_performed":["Installed mariadb, mariadb-client, galera, rsync on node1/node2/node3 via apk","Diagnosed and fixed a platform defect: Alpine's busybox ps/lsof applets lack -p/-i LISTEN support needed by wsrep_sst_rsync readiness checks, causing spurious rsync SST failures; installed real procps-ng, lsof, iproute2 packages to resolve the correct binaries via PATH","Configured /etc/my.cnf.d/galera.cnf on all three nodes with cluster address and per-node identity, rsync SST method","Bootstrapped Galera on node1 (--wsrep-new-cluster), joined node2 and node3 via SST, verified wsrep_cluster_size=3 and Synced state","Generated a root DB password on node1 via /dev/urandom (not exposed in this report), applied with ALTER USER, confirmed Galera-replicated grant tables took effect cluster-wide","Created appdb.orders table and inserted 3 committed rows on node1; verified replication to node2 and node3","Performed the maintenance-window full cluster shutdown: stopped node3, then node2, then node1 in that order to preserve highest seqno/safe_to_bootstrap on node1","Verified grastate.dat showed node1 seqno=10 safe_to_bootstrap=1, confirming correct shutdown order","Confirmed full outage: all three mariadbd processes down, no member reachable","Restarted the cluster: bootstrapped node1 (wsrep-new-cluster) confirming all 3 pre-shutdown rows present, then started node2 and node3 which rejoined via SST and reported Synced/cluster_size=3","Performed a post-recovery write test (INSERT on node2) and confirmed it replicated to node3, proving multi-master write availability restored","Executed mandatory node-restart evidence protocol: captured boot_id baseline on all 3 nodes, restarted node1 via native reboot (quorum preserved with node2+node3 up), polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, verified MariaDB auto-started and rejoined as Synced/cluster_size=3 with data intact","Repeated the restart cycle for node2 (quorum preserved by node1+node3), then node3 (quorum preserved by node1+node2), confirming boot_id change and full Galera rejoin with data intact after each","Performed a final cross-node consistency check from node1 confirming cluster_size=3, all three peer addresses present, and consistent row count (4) across the cluster"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Healthy 3-member Galera cluster established with committed application data","command_ids":["cmd-a746392e8438488f","cmd-03ddd375a1cd48cf","cmd-a70f66eb469341f0","cmd-2671e88ba0064262"],"summary":"Cluster reached wsrep_cluster_size=3, all Synced/Primary; appdb.orders table created with 3 committed rows on node1 and confirmed replicated to node2 and node3."},{"requirement":"Full cluster maintenance shutdown","command_ids":["cmd-e1fefb8356904a9a","cmd-931171aefabb44ea","cmd-dab5abb559f2484a","cmd-9fcb014b61674145","cmd-4aadc79e34a447c2","cmd-3b52399b484e46df"],"summary":"node3, node2, then node1 stopped in sequence (correct order); grastate.dat on each confirms clean shutdown with node1 holding the highest seqno (10) and safe_to_bootstrap=1, and all mysqladmin ping calls fail confirming full outage."},{"requirement":"Cluster brought back up with every committed write present and all three members serving","command_ids":["cmd-af62673609d14d09","cmd-a242fd70b01040ae","cmd-d5b866c159994c69","cmd-20b44b779dee41b4","cmd-39d40b77f1444835","cmd-e75bad6c04fa4bb2"],"summary":"node1 bootstrapped from its safe_to_bootstrap state showing all 3 pre-shutdown rows; node2 and node3 rejoined via SST reporting Synced/cluster_size=3 with the same rows; a post-recovery write on node2 replicated to node3; final check from node1 shows cluster_size=3 and consistent row count across all nodes."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-d828dc0e2a984027","cmd-d9b3f99bb1ae4e3b","cmd-ef64de8501314830","cmd-8dc060ce30694d6f"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 142a4fa7... captured; reboot acknowledged and returned before disconnect; post-restart boot_id a5693eca... confirms a real reboot; MariaDB auto-started and rejoined as Synced/cluster_size=3 with appdb.orders data intact."},{"requirement":"node2 mandatory restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-0f195b88b1a24d44","cmd-5e51de57834f4297","cmd-c930d56ecff449de","cmd-c03d7097f93a4707"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id ff2ab5bc... captured; reboot acknowledged; post-restart boot_id d27dcf53... confirms reboot; MariaDB auto-started and rejoined as Synced/cluster_size=3 with data intact, taken while node1+node3 preserved quorum."},{"requirement":"node3 mandatory restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-04d26292b6e1468e","cmd-b39feb61c12f4067","cmd-3e9b2401284341f2","cmd-07174e72a397434f"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id a9a825cc... captured; reboot acknowledged; post-restart boot_id 7957cd30... confirms reboot; MariaDB auto-started and rejoined as Synced/cluster_size=3/Primary with data intact, taken while node1+node2 preserved quorum."},{"requirement":"Root cause diagnosis and fix for Galera SST tooling defect on Alpine","command_ids":["cmd-e9ba168198b74380","cmd-887ffaa04c9e433b","cmd-ad7d203a8d274509","cmd-7730c365f9f743e3","cmd-8ca13a390bf94b32","cmd-292f3213b91f4494"],"summary":"Identified that busybox-provided ps/lsof (lacking -p and LISTEN-column support) broke wsrep_sst_rsync's readiness detection, causing false 'terminated unexpectedly' SST failures; installed procps-ng, lsof, and iproute2 on all three nodes to resolve real binaries via PATH, which fixed SST joins."}]},"ttft_ms":3368,"type":"result","duration_ms":774295,"uuid":"d81ead12-c462-4d6e-a027-af8b99765ff5","ttft_stream_ms":1696,"time_to_request_ms":50,"first_content_frame_ms":2729,"queued_turn_count":0}
